p.src:
If the elevator height is $h$, then to first order $\Delta t \simeq \frac{h}{c},
  \qquad
  \Delta v \simeq g\Delta t \simeq \frac{gh}{c}.$ The first-order Doppler shift is consequently $\frac{\Delta\nu}{\nu}
  \simeq
  \frac{\Delta v}{c}
  \simeq
  \frac{gh}{c^{2}}.$ For a downward ray this quantity is positive. Reversing the experiment reverses the sign: $\frac{\nu_{\mathrm{floor}}}{\nu_{\mathrm{roof}}}
  \simeq 1+\frac{gh}{c^{2}},
  \qquad
  \frac{\nu_{\mathrm{roof}}}{\nu_{\mathrm{floor}}}
  \simeq 1-\frac{gh}{c^{2}}.$

