Introduce another coordinate system, $y^{n}=y^{n}(x^{1},\ldots,x^{d}).$ An admissible change of coordinates is one-to-one on the region being used, differentiable, and equipped with a differentiable inverse. It relabels points; it does not change the dimension of the space. The chain rule gives $\boxed{
  \frac{\partial\phi}{\partial y^{n}}
  =
  \frac{\partial\phi}{\partial x^{m}}
  \frac{\partial x^{m}}{\partial y^{n}}.}$ For each free index $n$, the repeated index $m$ is summed.

