p.src:
The infinitesimal displacement is the model contravariant vector. Applying the total-differential rule to each coordinate function $y^{n}(x)$ gives $dy^{n}
  =
  \frac{\partial y^{n}}{\partial x^{m}}\,dx^{m}.$ Any contravariant vector transforms by the same rule: $\boxed{
  V_{(y)}^{n}
  =
  \frac{\partial y^{n}}{\partial x^{m}}\,V_{(x)}^{m}.}$

