p.src:
The gradient of a scalar transforms oppositely. Define $A_{m}^{(x)}
  =
  \frac{\partial\phi}{\partial x^{m}}.$ Equation  says $\boxed{
  A_{n}^{(y)}
  =
  \frac{\partial x^{m}}{\partial y^{n}}\,A_{m}^{(x)}.}$ This is a covariant vector, or covector. Contravariant components carry upper indices; covariant components carry lower indices.

