p.src:
Now change from $x$ to $y$. The differentials obey $dx^{m}
  =
  \frac{\partial x^{m}}{\partial y^{r}}\,dy^{r}.$ Substitution into Eq.  gives $\begin{aligned}
  ds^{2}
  &=
  \delta_{mn}
  \frac{\partial x^{m}}{\partial y^{r}}
  \frac{\partial x^{n}}{\partial y^{s}}
  dy^{r}dy^{s}
  \nonumber\\
  &=
  g_{rs}^{(y)}(y)\,dy^{r}dy^{s},
  \end{aligned}$ where $\boxed{
  g_{rs}^{(y)}(y)
  =
  \delta_{mn}
  \frac{\partial x^{m}}{\partial y^{r}}
  \frac{\partial x^{n}}{\partial y^{s}}.}$

