p.src:
More generally, if the metric in the $x$-coordinates is $g_{mn}^{(x)}$, then $\boxed{
  g_{rs}^{(y)}
  =
  g_{mn}^{(x)}
  \frac{\partial x^{m}}{\partial y^{r}}
  \frac{\partial x^{n}}{\partial y^{s}}.}$ The metric is therefore a rank-two covariant tensor. The number $ds^{2}$ is invariant, while the components $g_{mn}$ and $dx^{m}$ change in compensating ways.

