p.src:
Substituting and expanding, $\begin{aligned}
  ds^{2}
  &=
  dx^{2}+dy^{2}
  \nonumber\\
  &=
  \bigl(\cos\theta\,dr-r\sin\theta\,d\theta\bigr)^{2}
  \nonumber\\
  &\quad+
  \bigl(\sin\theta\,dr+r\cos\theta\,d\theta\bigr)^{2}
  \nonumber\\
  &=
  dr^{2}+r^{2}d\theta^{2}.
  \end{aligned}$ The mixed terms cancel. Thus $(g_{ab})
  =
  \begin{pmatrix}
    g_{rr} & g_{r\theta}\\
    g_{\theta r} & g_{\theta\theta}
  \end{pmatrix}
  =
  \begin{pmatrix}
    1 & 0\\
    0 & r^{2}
  \end{pmatrix}.$

